\title{The Corpus Algebra of the Attention Knee}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{2 September 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
Sparse-attention deployment rests on a single empirical number: the \emph{knee}, the
smallest key budget at which a sorted attention profile already retains a prescribed
fraction $\tau$ of its total mass. Measurements on transformer language models report a
strikingly stable knee --- roughly thirty keys, and specifically $\kstar = 16$ at context
$512$ and $\kstar = 32$ at context $1024$ --- which replicates \emph{exactly} across
independent text corpora, with control curves agreeing to four decimal places.

We give an algebraic theory that explains this stability and converts it into deployable
statements. The essential step is to write the gate condition in linear rather than ratio
form, $\tau M_w(n) \le M_w(k)$, so that it defines a half space in the cone of nonnegative
attention profiles. From this one reformulation we derive: (i) that the knee is a
scale-invariant, non-archimedean valuation on the corpus cone, with the sharp pooling
sandwich $\min \le \kstar(A+B) \le \max$ and exact equality on the diagonal; (ii) a
\emph{four-decimal theorem} showing that $\varepsilon$-agreement of two retention curves
forces exact equality of knees whenever the reference corpus keeps a gate margin exceeding
$\varepsilon$, together with a scale-free counterexample proving the margin hypothesis
necessary; (iii) a Galois duality between gates and budgets, under which the retention
curve is the upper envelope of the gate sweep and the sweep is a complete invariant of a
corpus's measurable content; (iv) a domain-jump law in which cross-domain distortion is
measured projectively --- a $\rho$-tilt inflates the \emph{missing mass} by exactly
$\rho^2$, yielding a gate window
$\kstar_A(\tau/\rho^2) \le \kstar_B(\tau) \le \kstar_A(\rho^2\tau)$ and, under a geometric
tail, a budget bound logarithmic in the distortion; and (v) a structure theorem exhibiting
the corpus cone as a \emph{knee fan}, partitioned into non-empty polyhedral cells each cut
out by exactly two linear measurements.

We also record a negative result of practical consequence: the knee is \textbf{not}
additive, and the pooled knee is not even a function of the ingredient knees. Explicit
two-key witnesses realise both endpoints of the sandwich for the \emph{same} pair of
corpora at different gates.
\end{abstract}

